{%- comment -%}
  Bundle Builder — interactive "build your box" section (Model B, multi-box).

  The shopper mixes flavours freely via per-flavour steppers. The packs are
  auto-chunked into boxes of BOX_CAPACITY (6) in add order; the total must be a
  multiple of 6 (no half-built box) before "Add to cart" unlocks. Each full box
  is added to the native Shopify cart as its own "Build Your Box" line item at
  the flat box price — boxes with an identical flavour mix merge into one line
  with quantity N. No discount tiers.

  Two standalone web components, communicating only via `bundle-v2:updated` on
  `document` (theme convention — see conventions/sections.md):

    <bundle-v2-builder> (assets/bundle-v2-builder.js)
      Owns the draft (flat ordered list of packs, no upper limit)
      + its localStorage persistence, the per-flavour steppers, the divisible-by-4
      gate, and "Add to cart". Reads the .bundle-v2-flavours JSON blob below for
      flavour name/notes/image.

    <bundle-v2-stage> (assets/bundle-v2-stage.js)
      Pure 2D PNG-compositing depth-stack visualiser (NO three.js). Listens for
      `bundle-v2:updated` and renders one scene per box (last may be partial),
      each stacking just the packs, newest at the front. Unlike v1 there is NO
      carton artwork — see BOX IMAGERY below. Scenes are cloned from a
      <template>; pack images ride along in the event detail.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DATA MODEL

  The box itself is ONE product (the "Build Your Box" product, priced at the
  flat box price) chosen in the section settings. On "Add to cart" the section
  POSTs one item per full box to /cart/add.js (with the box's flavours as
  line-item properties) — the native cart treats each as any other line item.

  Flavours are CURATED PER BOX PRODUCT: the box product's
  `custom.included_flavours` metafield (a list of `flavour` metaobjects) sets
  which flavours show and in what order. Each referenced flavour metaobject
  needs these field handles:

    name        single_line_text_field  — flavour name ("Mexi Fiesta Blend")
    atrributes  single_line_text_field  — descriptors ("Smoky • Rich • Peppery") (optional)
                                          (field-handle typo lives in Shopify; rename
                                          there to `attributes` and update this file)
    image       file_reference (image)   — the pouch render PNG for the visualiser
    sku         single_line_text_field  — the single-pack SKU, mirrored from the
                                          flavour's product variant. Stored here (NOT
                                          read from product_reference.value.variants)
                                          because the single-pack products are excluded
                                          from the Online Store channel, and Liquid
                                          cannot reach an off-channel product's variants
                                          via a metafield reference — the SKU collapses
                                          to "". The 3PL consumes this via the hidden
                                          `_bundle` line-item property, so it must be set.

  No box product (or an empty metafield) → no flavours render and add stays off.

  BOX IMAGERY — deliberately absent in v2. Where v1 composites the packs between
  a box-back and box-front render, this section draws the pack images alone: the
  scene is an empty square that only reserves space and sets the stack origin.
  While the draft is empty the stage carries `.is-empty` and a centred prompt
  (`sections.bundle_builder.empty_custom_box`) shows in its place, so the section
  never renders a bare box. The box-back/box-front image settings and the
  assets/box-back.png / box-front.png fallbacks are v1-only — don't reintroduce
  them here.

  PACKS ARE SOLD INDIVIDUALLY. There is no box quantum and no upper limit — the
  only constraint is an order MINIMUM of 6 packs, locked here (not a merchant
  setting). Above the minimum any quantity is addable.

  The box product's variant price must therefore be the SINGLE-PACK price; the
  whole draft goes to the cart as one line with quantity = the pack count. v1 is
  the older model — priced per box of 4, one line per full box — so the two
  sections are NOT interchangeable and their products are priced differently.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign min_packs = 6 -%}
{%- assign box_product = section.settings.box_product -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Prefer the available variant (for price + a clean add); fall back to the first
  variant so the add button stays live even when nothing is "available" — the
  /cart/add.js call then surfaces a real "out of stock" error instead of the
  button silently sitting disabled.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign box_variant = box_product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: box_product.variants.first -%}
{%- comment -%} Curated, ordered list of flavour metaobjects, set per box product. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign included_flavours = box_product.metafields.custom.included_flavours.value -%}

<bundle-v2-builder
  class="bundle-v2-builder{% if section.settings.full_screen %} full-screen{% endif %}"
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  data-min-packs="{{ min_packs }}"
  {% if box_variant %}data-box-variant-id="{{ box_variant.id }}"{% endif %}
  {%- comment -%} Per-PACK price — the variant price is the single-pack price. {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if box_variant %}data-box-price-cents="{{ box_variant.price }}"{% endif %}
  data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format }}"
  data-i18n-add="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.add_to_cart' | t }}"
  {%- comment -%} v2 counts up to the order minimum, not to a full box — its own key. {%- endcomment -%}
  data-i18n-add-more="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.add_minimum' | t }}"
  data-i18n-added="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.added' | t: product: box_product.title }}"
  data-i18n-error="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.checkout_error' | t }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    Visible line-item property stamped on every blend line, marking it as part of
    the custom box. Visible (no leading underscore) so it carries through cart,
    checkout and the order confirmation; it is also what the cart groups on.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  data-box-property-key="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.box_property_key' | t }}"
  data-box-property-value="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.box_property_value' | t }}"
>
  <script type="application/json" class="bundle-v2-flavours">
    [
      {%- for flavour in included_flavours -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Each flavour must resolve to a PURCHASABLE variant — v2 adds the blends
          themselves to the cart, one line each, rather than a single box line.

          These are the real single-pack products, via the flavour metaobject's
          `product_reference`. NOTE they must be published to the ONLINE STORE
          sales channel: while they aren't, Liquid sees the reference as blank,
          `variantId` comes through null, and add-to-cart stays disabled — the
          section degrades rather than posting a variant /cart/add.js would
          reject. (A dev stand-in that borrowed the published Box products lived
          here until 2026-08-26; see git history if it's needed again.)
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign flavour_product = flavour.product_reference.value -%}
        {%- assign flavour_variant = flavour_product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: flavour_product.variants.first -%}
        {
          "id": {{ flavour.system.handle | json }},
          "name": {{ flavour.name.value | json }},
          "attributes": {{ flavour.atrributes.value | default: '' | json }},
          "image": {% if flavour.image.value != blank %}{{ flavour.image.value | image_url: width: 1500 | json }}{% else %}""{% endif %},
          "sku": {{ flavour.sku.value | default: '' | json }},
          {%- comment -%} `| append: ''` casts the colour object to its hex string; `| json` alone rejects it. {%- endcomment -%}
          "colour": {{ flavour.dark_colour | append: '' | json }},
          "variantId": {% if flavour_variant %}{{ flavour_variant.id | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
          "priceCents": {% if flavour_variant %}{{ flavour_variant.price }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
          {%- comment -%}
            Each blend's OWN selling plans. A selling plan id is only valid for
            variants in its own group, and Recharge may well have made a separate
            group per product — so the plan is matched across blends by NAME and
            each line is posted with its own id. Never reuse one blend's id for
            another, and never reuse the box product's.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          "plans": [
            {%- for allocation in flavour_variant.selling_plan_allocations -%}
              {
                "name": {{ allocation.selling_plan.name | json }},
                "id": {{ allocation.selling_plan.id | json }},
                "priceCents": {{ allocation.price }},
                "compareCents": {{ allocation.compare_at_price | default: allocation.price }}
              }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  </script>

  <div class="bundle-v2-layout">
    <section class="bundle-v2-panel">
      <header class="section-lockup">
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <h1 class="text-h1">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</h1>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="text-h3">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
      </header>

      <div class="bundle-v2-flavour-list" data-flavour-list>
        {%- for flavour in included_flavours -%}
          <article
            class="bundle-v2-flavour"
            data-flavour-card
            data-flavour-id="{{ flavour.system.handle }}"
            {%- if flavour.dark_colour != blank or flavour.light_colour != blank -%}
              style="
                {%- if flavour.dark_colour != blank -%}--flavour-dark: {{ flavour.dark_colour }};{%- endif -%}
                {%- if flavour.light_colour != blank -%}--flavour-light: {{ flavour.light_colour }};{%- endif -%}
              "
            {%- endif -%}
          >
            <div class="bundle-v2-flavour-header">
              <div class="bundle-v2-flavour-title">
                <h3 class="text-ui">{{ flavour.name }}</h3>
                {%- if flavour.atrributes != blank -%}
                  <p class="bundle-v2-flavour-attributes">{{ flavour.atrributes }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              {%- assign flavour_product = flavour.product_reference.value -%}
              {%- if flavour_product != blank -%}
                <a
                  class="bundle-v2-flavour-link"
                  href="{{ flavour_product.url }}"
                  aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.view_product' | t: name: flavour.name }}"
                >
                  <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 7 7" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M0.753846 7L0 6.24615L5.16923 1.07692H0.538462V0H7V6.46154H5.92308V1.83077L0.753846 7Z"/>
                  </svg>
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            <div class="bundle-v2-stepper">
              <button
                type="button"
                data-action="remove"
                data-flavour-id="{{ flavour.system.handle }}"
                aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.decrease' | t: name: flavour.name }}"
                disabled
              >
                <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 7 1" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                  <path d="M0 1V0H7V1H0Z"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <span class="bundle-v2-qty" data-qty="{{ flavour.system.handle }}">0</span>
              <button
                type="button"
                data-action="add"
                data-flavour-id="{{ flavour.system.handle }}"
                aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.increase' | t: name: flavour.name }}"
              >
                <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 7 7" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                  <path d="M3 4H0V3H3V0H4V3H7V4H4V7H3V4Z"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          </article>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="bundle-v2-flavour-attributes">{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.no_flavours' | t }}</p>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      <footer class="bundle-v2-footer">
        {%- comment -%}
          Subscription control. Built from the BLENDS, not the box — the box is no
          longer purchased, and its plan ids would be rejected on a blend line.

          The frequency list comes from the first flavour that has plans; on
          add-to-cart bundle-v2-builder.js looks the chosen frequency up by NAME
          in each blend's own plan list, so every line carries a plan id valid for
          its own variant. A frequency not offered by every blend is dropped from
          the list by the JS.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign plan_source = blank -%}
        {%- for flavour in included_flavours -%}
          {%- assign candidate = flavour.product_reference.value -%}
          {%- assign candidate_variant = candidate.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: candidate.variants.first -%}
          {%- if candidate_variant.selling_plan_allocations.size > 0 -%}
            {%- assign plan_source = candidate_variant -%}
            {%- break -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- if plan_source != blank -%}
          {%- assign box_alloc = plan_source.selling_plan_allocations | first -%}
          {%- assign box_discount = box_alloc.compare_at_price | minus: box_alloc.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: box_alloc.compare_at_price | round -%}
          <div class="bundle-v2-subscription" data-subscription>
            <fieldset class="bundle-v2-sub-options">
              <legend class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.purchase_options' | t }}</legend>

              <label class="bundle-v2-sub-option is-selected">
                <input type="radio" name="bundle-v2-purchase-{{ section.id }}" value="onetime" checked data-sub-mode>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-label text-ui">{{ 'products.product.one_time' | t }}</span>
              </label>

              <label class="bundle-v2-sub-option">
                <input type="radio" name="bundle-v2-purchase-{{ section.id }}" value="subscription" data-sub-mode>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="bundle-v2-sub-label text-ui">{{ 'products.product.subscribe_save' | t: percent: box_discount }}</span>
              </label>
            </fieldset>

            <div class="bundle-v2-sub-frequency" data-sub-frequency hidden>
              <label class="visually-hidden" for="bundle-v2-frequency-{{ section.id }}">{{ 'products.product.deliver_every' | t }}</label>
              <select id="bundle-v2-frequency-{{ section.id }}" class="select bundle-v2-sub-select text-ui" data-sub-select>
                {%- comment -%} value is the plan NAME — the key that maps across blends. {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- for allocation in plan_source.selling_plan_allocations -%}
                  <option value="{{ allocation.selling_plan.name | escape }}">
                    {{ allocation.selling_plan.name | split: ' subscription' | first }}
                  </option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <button type="button" class="button bundle-v2-add" data-add disabled>
          <span class="bundle-v2-add-inner">
            <span class="bundle-v2-add-label" data-add-label>{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.add_to_cart' | t }}</span>
            <span class="bundle-v2-add-end">
              {%- if box_variant -%}
                <s class="bundle-v2-add-was" data-add-was hidden></s>
                {%- comment -%} Empty-state preview: the minimum order, matching updateAddPrice(). {%- endcomment -%}
                  <span class="bundle-v2-add-price">{{ box_variant.price | times: min_packs | money }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {% render 'icon-arrow', class: 'bundle-v2-add-icon' %}
            </span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <p class="bundle-v2-hint" data-hint aria-live="polite"></p>

        <div class="bundle-v2-progress" data-progress role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="{{ min_packs }}" aria-valuenow="0">
          <div class="bundle-v2-progress-fill" data-progress-fill></div>
        </div>

        <div class="form-error" data-error role="alert" hidden></div>
      </footer>
    </section>

    <div class="bundle-v2-visualiser">
      <bundle-v2-stage class="bundle-v2-stage">
        {%- comment -%}
          Scroll controls flank the fan: back on the left, forward on the right,
          both vertically centred by the stage's own `align-items: center`. They
          keep their space when the fan fits (hidden, not removed) so crossing the
          overflow threshold doesn't shift the layout.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="bundle-v2-nav-button"
          data-scroll="back"
          aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.scroll_back' | t }}"
        >
          {% render 'icon-arrow', class: 'bundle-v2-nav-icon is-back' %}
        </button>

        <div class="bundle-v2-stage-track" data-stage></div>
        {%- comment -%}
          The single row of pouches, cloned from this template by bundle-v2-stage.js.
          The whole draft is ONE continuous fan — it never wraps and boxes are not
          expressed visually; the track scrolls instead. The element is an empty
          frame; the stage sets --n on it and appends the pack slots.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <template data-box-template>
          <div class="bundle-v2-row" data-scene></div>
        </template>

        {%- comment -%}
          Shown while the draft is empty; bundle-v2-stage.js toggles `.is-empty` on
          the host. Overlays the reserved scene square rather than replacing it, so
          nothing reflows when the first pack lands.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="bundle-v2-empty text-h3">{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.empty_custom_box' | t }}</p>

        <button
          type="button"
          class="bundle-v2-nav-button"
          data-scroll="forward"
          aria-label="{{ 'sections.bundle_builder.scroll_forward' | t }}"
        >
          {% render 'icon-arrow', class: 'bundle-v2-nav-icon' %}
        </button>
      </bundle-v2-stage>
    </div>
  </div>
</bundle-v2-builder>

{% stylesheet %}
  .bundle-v2-builder {
    display: block;
    padding: var(--spacing-xs);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Phones-only: bump top/bottom for a touch more vertical breathing room. */
  @media (max-width: 599.98px) {
    .bundle-v2-builder {
      padding-block: var(--spacing-m);
    }
  }

  .bundle-v2-layout {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
    gap: var(--spacing-m);
    align-items: center;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-l);
  }

  /* Builder panel */
  .bundle-v2-panel {
    /* Positioned so .bundle-v2-progress can anchor to the panel's outer edges
       (left / right / bottom) and break out of the panel's inner padding. */
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-m);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 460px;
    padding: var(--spacing-xs);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-dark);
  }

  /* Cap the panel's section heading at 36ch — matches the rest of the theme.
     Scoped via direct child of the lockup so the per-card flavour h3 stays
     unconstrained. */
  .bundle-v2-panel > .section-lockup h3 {
    max-width: 36ch;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--spacing-xxxs);
  }

  /* Flavour card + stepper.
     Local tokens (--c-text / --c-text-accent / --c-bg) so the .is-active state
     can swap to the flavour's dark_colour + light_colour without re-stating
     every rule. Defaults map to the theme tokens; the active state overrides. */
  .bundle-v2-flavour {
    --c-text: var(--color-text);
    --c-text-accent: var(--color-text-accent);
    --c-bg: var(--color-bg);
    --c-surface-muted: var(--color-bg-dark);

    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--spacing-m);
    padding: var(--spacing-xxs);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background: var(--c-bg);
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour.is-active {
    --c-text: var(--flavour-dark, var(--color-text));
    --c-text-accent: color-mix(in srgb, var(--flavour-dark, var(--color-text)) 50%, transparent);
    /* Same dark @ 50% transparent as the attributes line — applied as bg for
       the muted buttons (disabled stepper + expand link). */
    --c-surface-muted: color-mix(in srgb, var(--flavour-dark, var(--color-text)) 50%, transparent);
    /* Light colour @ 50% composited over --color-bg (off-white), rendered as
       one opaque value so the result doesn't bleed through to the panel's
       beige bg. Equivalent to 0.5 × light + 0.5 × bg. */
    --c-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--flavour-light, var(--color-bg)) 50%, var(--color-bg));
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-title {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-title h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-link {
    flex: none;
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--c-surface-muted);
    color: var(--c-text);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast), color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-link:hover,
  .bundle-v2-flavour-link:focus-visible {
    background-color: var(--c-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .bundle-v2-flavour-attributes {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--type-mini-size);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-text-accent, var(--color-text-accent));
  }

  .bundle-v2-stepper {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxxs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-stepper button {
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    padding: 0;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--c-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stepper button:disabled {
    background-color: var(--c-surface-muted);
    color: var(--c-text);
    cursor: default;
  }

  .bundle-v2-qty {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-width: 24px;
    font-size: var(--type-mini-size);
  }

  /* Footer: add button (carries the flat box price) + progress bar */
  .bundle-v2-footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    /* Pull the footer up so the gap from the flavour list reads as s, not the
       panel's m (one step smaller between the cards and the subscription). */
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing-s) - var(--spacing-m));
  }

  /* Dark variant of the primary .button: same shape/type as .button but with
     a muted bg until the box is full. Hover inverts to yellow on dark.
     One step up from the .button label size (h1 12px → ui 14px) so this
     primary CTA reads larger than a standard button. */
  .bundle-v2-add {
    width: 100%;
    font-size: var(--type-ui-size);
    background-color: var(--color-text-accent);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    transition:
      background-color var(--transition-fast),
      color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  /* When the box is full (= button enabled), bg shifts to the brand dark. */
  .bundle-v2-add:not(:disabled) {
    background-color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-add:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Disabled-until-full state: keep the button visible (the progress bar below
     signals the build-up) but override .button:disabled's 0.6 opacity so the
     muted bg colour does the "not yet" signalling on its own. */
  .bundle-v2-add:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* Inner flex wrapper — keep .button as inline-block per the convention; flex
     an inner span when an icon + label need laying out side-by-side. */
  .bundle-v2-add-inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-s);
  }

  /* Price + forward arrow, pinned to the button's trailing edge. */
  .bundle-v2-add-end {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  /* 2px of padding-bottom nudges the arrow's bounding box up by ~1px within
     the centered flex row — optically aligns it with the cap-line of the
     all-caps label/price (compensates for the font's bottom-heavy baseline). */
  .bundle-v2-add-icon {
    padding-bottom: 2px;
  }

  /* Original (pre-discount) total, struck through — shown by JS for
     subscriptions next to the discounted total. */
  .bundle-v2-add-was {
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }

  .bundle-v2-add-was[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Build hint — nudges the shopper to finish the in-progress box. Reserves a
     line so the footer doesn't jump as the text toggles on/off. */
  .bundle-v2-hint {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 1.2em;
    font-size: var(--type-mini-size);
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
  }

  /* Progress bar — thin track + fill that tracks the IN-PROGRESS box (the
     partial last box), so it fills 0→100% per box. Anchored to the panel's
     outer left/right/bottom edges so it sits as a flush bar on the container,
     ignoring the panel's inner padding. The fill width is set inline by
     bundle-v2-builder.js render() as total / minimum. */
  .bundle-v2-progress {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    height: 4px;
    background-color: var(--color-text-accent);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .bundle-v2-progress-fill {
    width: 0;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: var(--color-text);
    transition: width var(--transition-slow);
  }

  /* Valid selection (every box full) — fill is pinned to 100% and shifts to the
     brand accent to signal "ready to add". */
  .bundle-v2-progress.is-complete .bundle-v2-progress-fill {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* Visualiser */
  /* min-width: 0 on both this and the stage is load-bearing: flex items default
     to min-width: auto, which lets them expand to their content — the over-wide
     fan would stretch the column instead of scrolling inside it. */
  .bundle-v2-visualiser {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 460px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage {
    --pack-max: 340px;
    --step: 0.095;
    --pack-size: var(--pack-max);
    /* Depth dimming — each pouch further back in the fan is dimmed by another
       --pack-dim-step, bottoming out at --pack-dim-min. Since the fan is pinned
       right, the deepest pouches are the ones running off the left edge, so this
       shades the cut-off end without any overlay.

       Tuned so the ramp finishes within THREE pouches (1.0 → 0.92 → 0.84 → 0.76)
       and everything deeper sits flat at the floor — a short, shallow falloff
       reads as depth without turning the tail of the fan murky. */
    --pack-dim-step: 0.08;
    --pack-dim-min: 0.76;
    /* Where the drawn pouch sits inside its square render, as a fraction of the
       frame. The pouch is authored against the RIGHT of the frame (so the fan
       can stack leftwards), leaving a wide transparent margin on the left — 38%
       of the frame. Without discounting it the row box would start 38% of a
       pouch before the first visible pixel, opening a dead gap at the start.
       Measured off the artwork (opaque box 573..1361 x, 161..1392 y of 1500) and
       verified identical across all four flavour renders. Re-measure if the
       renders are re-exported. */
    --art-top: 0.107;
    --art-right: 0.092;
    --art-bottom: 0.071;
    --art-left: 0.382;
    /* [ back ] [ fan ] [ forward ] — align-items centres the arrows against the
       pouch container rather than stacking them below it. */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    /* Keep the pack z-indexes local — without a stacking context the stacked
       packs' z-index would leak to the root and paint over the cart drawer
       (z-index 99). */
    isolation: isolate;
  }

  /* Empty state — centred over the reserved scene square. */
  .bundle-v2-empty {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--spacing-s);
    color: var(--color-text-light);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage:not(.is-empty) .bundle-v2-empty {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The fan's viewport. Pouches keep a constant size, so a long draft simply
     outgrows this box and scrolls — bundle-v2-stage.js pins the right edge (the
     newest pouch) after every update. Block rather than flex: a flex container
     centring an over-wide child clips its left end unreachably in a scroller,
     whereas `margin: 0 auto` on the row collapses to 0 when there's no free
     space and centres when there is. */
  .bundle-v2-stage-track {
    display: block;
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
    cursor: grab;
    /* Scrollbar hidden — browsing is via the arrows and click-drag below. */
    scrollbar-width: none;
    /* Horizontal only. `overflow-x: auto` forces the other axis to compute to
       auto too, and the pouches' enter/exit transforms (translateY) push a few
       pixels of scrollable overflow — enough to flash a vertical scrollbar. The
       block padding gives those transforms room so hiding clips nothing. */
    overflow-y: hidden;
    padding-block: var(--spacing-xxs);
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage-track::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-stage.is-dragging .bundle-v2-stage-track {
    cursor: grabbing;
    /* Kill text/image selection mid-drag. */
    user-select: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-nav-button {
    flex: none;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    padding: 0;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast), color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .bundle-v2-nav-button:hover:not(:disabled) {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-nav-button:disabled {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-dark);
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
    cursor: default;
  }

  /* Nothing to scroll: keep the footprint, drop the dead controls. */
  .bundle-v2-stage:not(.is-scrollable) .bundle-v2-nav-button {
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .bundle-v2-nav-icon.is-back {
    transform: scaleX(-1);
  }

  /* The fan itself. Width is exactly its span, so it centres while it fits and
     scrolls once it doesn't. --n (the pack count) is set by the stage. */
  /* Sized to the VISIBLE artwork, not the square slots — the row's edges land on
     the first and last drawn pixel, so the fan starts flush against the back
     arrow and the stage reserves no dead space. The slots hang outside this box
     (see below); their overhang is transparent. */
  .bundle-v2-row {
    --n: 1;
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 auto;
    width: calc(
      var(--pack-size) *
        ((1 + var(--step) * (var(--n) - 1)) - var(--art-left) - var(--art-right))
    );
    height: calc(var(--pack-size) * (1 - var(--art-top) - var(--art-bottom)));
  }

  /* The newest pouch sits flush to the row's right edge at identity; older ones
     translate left by their depth. */
  /* Offset by the artwork's own margin so the newest pouch's drawn right edge —
     not its transparent frame — sits flush with the row's right edge. */
  .bundle-v2-slot {
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(var(--pack-size) * var(--art-top) * -1);
    right: calc(var(--pack-size) * var(--art-right) * -1);
    width: var(--pack-size);
    height: var(--pack-size);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-pack {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .bundle-v2-pack {
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  /* A slot carries the depth transform; the inner pack carries enter/exit. */
  .bundle-v2-slot {
    transform-origin: 50% 82%;
    transition: transform 0.32s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  }

  /* --depth is written per-slot by bundle-v2-stage.js (0 = newest/front) and
     inherits to the image. Brightness first so the drop-shadow isn't dimmed
     along with the artwork. */
  .bundle-v2-pack {
    filter:
      brightness(clamp(var(--pack-dim-min), calc(1 - var(--depth, 0) * var(--pack-dim-step)), 1))
      drop-shadow(0 4px 8px var(--color-shadow-soft));
  }

  /* Scrolled back through the fan: drop the dimming so the pouches being
     inspected are all shown at full brightness. Adding re-pins to the front,
     which clears `is-browsing` and brings the depth shading back. */
  .bundle-v2-stage.is-browsing .bundle-v2-pack {
    filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 8px var(--color-shadow-soft));
    /* filter is deliberately NOT transitioned — it would animate on every depth
       change, and a paused/background tab freezes the transition at its start
       value, leaving pouches stuck undimmed. The dim is a state, not a motion. */
    transition:
      transform 0.34s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1),
      opacity 0.34s ease;
  }

  .bundle-v2-slot.is-entering .bundle-v2-pack {
    transform: translateY(-12%);
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-slot.is-leaving .bundle-v2-pack {
    transform: translateY(-8%);
    opacity: 0;
    transition-duration: 0.18s;
  }

  /* Desktop: builder left, visualiser fills remaining space and centers the scene */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .bundle-v2-builder {
      padding: var(--spacing-m);
    }

    .bundle-v2-layout {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: stretch;
      justify-content: flex-start;
      gap: var(--spacing-xl);
    }

    .bundle-v2-panel {
      flex: none;
      width: 440px;
      max-width: 440px;
      gap: var(--spacing-l);
      justify-content: space-between;
    }

    .bundle-v2-visualiser {
      flex: 1;
      max-width: none;
    }

    /* Roomier pouches on desktop, where the visualiser has the width. */
    .bundle-v2-stage {
      --pack-max: 560px;
    }

    .bundle-v2-flavour-list {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    /* Full-screen toggle (in section settings): adds extra vertical breathing
       room above and below the builder on desktop so the visualiser has room
       to breathe in a dedicated bundle page. Steps up at 1500px (`large`).
       Horizontal padding stays at the default --spacing-m. Mobile + tablet
       are untouched. */
    .bundle-v2-builder.full-screen {
      padding-top: var(--spacing-l);
      padding-bottom: var(--spacing-l);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1500px) {
    .bundle-v2-builder.full-screen {
      padding-top: var(--spacing-xl);
      padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    }
  }

  /* Dev-only calibration overlay (toggle with ?bundle-v2-calibrate in the URL) */
  .bundle-v2-calib {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 400;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxxs);
    width: 220px;
    padding: var(--spacing-xxs);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--type-mini-size);
  }

  .bundle-v2-calib label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .bundle-v2-calib input[type='range'] {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .bundle-v2-calib code {
    word-break: break-all;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .bundle-v2-slot,
    .bundle-v2-pack {
      transition: none;
    }

  }
  /* Subscription control — mirrors the PDP selector (snippets/product-subscription). */
  .bundle-v2-subscription {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-dark);
    border-radius: var(--rad-m);
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-options {
    border: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option input[type="radio"] {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-box {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-text);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background-color: transparent;
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option input:checked ~ .bundle-v2-sub-box {
    background-color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-option input:focus-visible ~ .bundle-v2-sub-box {
    outline: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-label {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-frequency {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .bundle-v2-sub-select {
    width: 100%;
    padding: var(--spacing-xxs) var(--spacing-m) var(--spacing-xxs) var(--spacing-xxs);
    color: var(--color-text);
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 14%, var(--color-bg-dark));
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .bundle-v2-sub-box {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

<script type="module" src="{{ 'bundle-v2-builder.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
<script type="module" src="{{ 'bundle-v2-stage.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Bundle builder (v2)",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "bundle-v2-builder-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "box_product",
      "label": "Box product",
      "info": "The single 'Build Your Box' product, priced at the flat box price. The chosen flavours are added to this product as a line-item property."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Flavours come from this product's 'Included flavours' metafield (custom.included_flavours) — a list of flavour metaobjects. Reorder there to reorder the cards. Each flavour needs a name, optional attributes, and an image. IMPORTANT: this product's price must be the SINGLE-PACK price — packs are sold individually with a 6-pack order minimum."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Header"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "Build your box"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Create and customise your box from the Frood selection."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "full_screen",
      "label": "Full screen section",
      "default": false,
      "info": "On desktop (≥900px), adds extra vertical padding (top + bottom) so the section feels more spacious — useful on a dedicated bundle page. Mobile and tablet are unaffected."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Bundle builder (v2)"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
